# AI Agent Instructions

Project: {{ project_name }}

This is the canonical shared instruction file. Keep client-specific files as
references to it, without duplicating instructions.

- Read applicable repository documentation and local process instructions before
  changing anything. Use them as the source of truth; report gaps or conflicts.
- Distinguish observed facts, proposals, accepted owner decisions and open
  questions. A recommendation is not an accepted decision.
- Obtain owner approval for material product, architecture, dependency, process
  or scope decisions unless already authorized. Make routine implementation
  choices within the agreed scope; do not assume a stack or deployment model.
- Keep changes focused on the request. Preserve unrelated work and each
  generated project's independence; do not add workflow machinery by default.
- Run the relevant documented checks and proportionate verification. Report
  what changed, results, limitations and unresolved questions; do not claim
  checks passed when they were not run.
- Deliver changes on a working branch through a pull request. The owner controls
  acceptance and merge; do not merge automatically.
- Never commit or expose credentials or secrets in code, logs, examples or PRs.
  Use the repository's documented secret handling; ask if required access is
  missing, and do not bypass access restrictions.
